  "notes": "Governmental funds cash basis (Total Governmental Funds column p5); business-type accrual (proprietary Totals column p8; disbursements 922,390 = operating 886,061 + interest 36,329, printed on the Statement of Activities p3). Business-type roll-forward: 4,412,521 + 997,504 - 922,390 + contributed capital 93,335 = 4,580,970. Governmental roll-forward uses cash basis fund balances (783,257 + 1,156,877 - 1,096,351 = 843,783); no single governmental cash total is printed (assets are pooled cash, cash equivalents, county treasurer, CDs and restricted cash), so beginning/ending cash left null. No actual transfers (budgeted transfers in/out show '-' actual and are skipped). Capital Outlay 5,496 has no printed function (Statement of Activities folds it into Public Works), so labelled 'Capital Outlay'. Proprietary Statement of Cash Flows Totals column p9; long-term debt proceeds 111,000 appear only in the cash flow statement. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement p4 (totals 843,783 equal the government-wide governmental column p1), business-type lines from p1; proprietary interfund due to/from 137,946 is eliminated on p1. Component unit (Ponderosa Villa) excluded. Detail: General, Streets and Keno budgetary comparison schedules (Actual column, pp10-12); the Keno schedule prints no total disbursements line (single line 3,001). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
